Make the build/ scripts GYP invokes Python 3 compatible.

GYP calls two scripts out of build/ during generation, and both are Python 2:

  build/win_is_xtree_patched.py   via <!pymod_do_main(win_is_xtree_patched)>,
                                  unconditionally (common.gypi sets
                                  msvs_xtree_patched from it)
  build/win/use_ansi_codes.py     via <!(python ...) inside a condition
                                  *expression*, which GYP expands before it
                                  evaluates the condition -- so this runs even
                                  though the condition itself is clang==1 and
                                  we build with MSVC

Each needs only its print statement parenthesised. Note the first fails even
though the offending line sits under `if __name__ == '__main__'`: pymod_do_main
imports the module, so the SyntaxError aborts the whole compile.

Python 2 reached end of life in 2020 and is not available here; see
tools/gyp_sawbuck.py for the rest of the Python 3 story.

--- a/build/win_is_xtree_patched.py
+++ b/build/win_is_xtree_patched.py
@@ -23,4 +23,4 @@
 
 
 if __name__ == '__main__':
-  print DoMain([])
+  print(DoMain([]))
--- a/build/win/use_ansi_codes.py
+++ b/build/win/use_ansi_codes.py
@@ -7,4 +7,4 @@
 import os
 
 # Add more terminals here as needed.
-print 'ANSICON' in os.environ
+print('ANSICON' in os.environ)
